  "question": {
    "text": "Given below are two statements:\nStatement I : D-glucose pentaacetate reacts with 2, 4-dinitrophenylhydrazine\nStatement II : Starch, on heating with concentrated sulfuric acid at $100^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ and 2-3 atmosphere pressure produces glucose.\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "bso5m",
      "text": "Statement I is false but Statement II is true",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ls9LV",
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "pH814",
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2LSPF",
      "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "- D-glucose pentaacetate do not react with 2.4 DNP\n- Starch $\\frac{\\text { conc. } \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{SO}_4}{\\Delta}$ Glucose\n$\\begin{gathered}2-3 \\mathrm{~atm} \\\\ 100^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}\\end{gathered}$",
